# apps/api deploy ids — copy to `.deploy.env`, which scripts/deploy.sh loads automatically.
#
#   cp apps/api/.deploy.env.example apps/api/.deploy.env
#
# These are NOT secrets and NOT runtime configuration: no Worker ever reads them. They are the
# account-specific ids of the resources `wrangler.jsonc` names with placeholders, and deploy.sh
# substitutes each one into a throwaway config just before it uploads. They stay out of git for a
# different reason than secrets do — a real id committed here points every clone, and every fork,
# at one person's database. In CI they are repository variables, not a file.
#
# Create the resources once per Cloudflare account:
#
#   bunx wrangler d1 create kothanote-db-dev
#   bunx wrangler d1 create kothanote-db-prod
#   dashboard -> Workers & Pages -> Feature flags: one Flagship app per environment
#
# A separate Flagship app per environment is the point of the release model: sharing one would
# make every flag flipped in dev a production release.
#
# Anything unset, still zeroes, or the wrong shape stops the deploy with the variable named —
# before anything is uploaded.

GC_DEV_D1_DATABASE_ID=""
GC_DEV_FLAGSHIP_APP_ID=""

GC_PROD_D1_DATABASE_ID=""
GC_PROD_FLAGSHIP_APP_ID=""
